<RCC>
  <!--
    Paths here point at WORKING COPIES under assets/interface/ and
    assets/branding/, named for the control they drive. The untouched design
    package is assets/source/original-design-package/ and nothing embeds from
    it directly; assets/README.md states the rule and why.

    ONE icon source. Before spec phase 2 there were three packages in the tree:
    assets/icons/ (app icon), assets/Interface/ (first-pass player icons) and
    the 260807 package, which supersedes both and says so in its own
    CONTENTS.txt. Both of the others are gone. Note the first-pass set was
    never actually needed as a separate directory, because the approved package
    carries a byte-identical copy of it as player-icons/, labelled SUPERSEDED
    and kept for reference. That is where the two frame-step glyphs below come
    from now.
  -->
  <qresource prefix="/icons">
    <file alias="trace-16.png">../assets/branding/app-icon/png/windows/trace-16.png</file>
    <file alias="trace-32.png">../assets/branding/app-icon/png/windows/trace-32.png</file>
    <file alias="trace-48.png">../assets/branding/app-icon/png/windows/trace-48.png</file>
    <file alias="trace-256.png">../assets/branding/app-icon/png/windows/trace-256.png</file>
  </qresource>

  <!--
    Transport icons. Only controls that exist in the app are embedded; the rest
    of the base UI set (volume, share, inspector, zoom, rotate, loop, ...) is
    deliberately left out until those features are real, which is why
    assets/interface/common/ is an empty directory rather than a populated one.

    The approved set ships 24px @1x and 48px @2x. It has no @3x, so a 3x display
    scales the 48px master rather than picking a dedicated file; the previous
    first-pass set did have one, which is why the two frame-step glyphs below
    are the only ones with a -72. SVG masters sit beside each PNG in
    assets/interface/ if that ever matters, but using them needs Qt6::Svg, which
    Trace does not link.

    THE TWO FRAME-STEP GLYPHS ARE STILL FROM THE OLD SET, ON PURPOSE. The
    approved package contains no frame-step icon by design ("Left/Right Arrow
    handle single frames"); its transport_scan_* pair is the artwork for the
    redesigned Rewind and Fast-forward, and those buttons still perform
    single-frame stepping until spec phases 4 and 5. Shipping the scan artwork
    over stepping behaviour would put a lie on a visible control in a player
    whose third pillar is that it can be trusted, so the artwork moves when the
    behaviour does. That is also when the two files leave assets/interface/.

    rewind/fast-forward ARE transport_scan_reverse/transport_scan_forward,
    renamed to what they do. They are embedded now, and unused, so phases 4 and
    5 are a code change only.
  -->
  <qresource prefix="/ui">
    <file alias="play-24.png">../assets/interface/transport/play-24.png</file>
    <file alias="play-48.png">../assets/interface/transport/play-48.png</file>

    <file alias="pause-24.png">../assets/interface/transport/pause-24.png</file>
    <file alias="pause-48.png">../assets/interface/transport/pause-48.png</file>

    <file alias="fullscreen-24.png">../assets/interface/window/fullscreen-enter-24.png</file>
    <file alias="fullscreen-48.png">../assets/interface/window/fullscreen-enter-48.png</file>

    <file alias="exit-fullscreen-24.png">../assets/interface/window/fullscreen-exit-24.png</file>
    <file alias="exit-fullscreen-48.png">../assets/interface/window/fullscreen-exit-48.png</file>

    <!-- Unused until spec phases 4 and 5 re-point the two side controls. -->
    <file alias="fast-forward-24.png">../assets/interface/transport/fast-forward-24.png</file>
    <file alias="fast-forward-48.png">../assets/interface/transport/fast-forward-48.png</file>

    <file alias="rewind-24.png">../assets/interface/transport/rewind-24.png</file>
    <file alias="rewind-48.png">../assets/interface/transport/rewind-48.png</file>

    <file alias="prev-frame-24.png">../assets/interface/transport/prev-frame-24.png</file>
    <file alias="prev-frame-48.png">../assets/interface/transport/prev-frame-48.png</file>
    <file alias="prev-frame-72.png">../assets/interface/transport/prev-frame-72.png</file>

    <file alias="next-frame-24.png">../assets/interface/transport/next-frame-24.png</file>
    <file alias="next-frame-48.png">../assets/interface/transport/next-frame-48.png</file>
    <file alias="next-frame-72.png">../assets/interface/transport/next-frame-72.png</file>
  </qresource>
</RCC>
